#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078129 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "98fdea06-a5ad-5d22-b928-ef893424e447" :question/math-academy-id "e-158" :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $1.1$ | $1.3$ | $1.7$ | $2.5$ |\n\nApproximate $f'(x)$ at the point $x=0.2$ using a central difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=0.2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0.2) & ≈\\frac{f(0.2+0.1)-f(0.2-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0.3)-f(0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.7-1.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.6}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078130 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "62934fda-d972-50d5-acdb-e1f7b2fd63f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-159" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/5355859a0307e46ae84d12bc5e0b183d72458972c8a417fb6d9296b4769ea078.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\dfrac{g(x+h) - g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+4)-g(4-4)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(8)-g(0)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-(-10)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078133 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "d405fda1-1111-56db-ae34-4c0f257852f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-160" :question/problem "A car engine is being heated from a temperature of about $-10^{\\circ}.$ The temperature of the engine after $t$ minutes is given by $T(t).$  The graph of $T(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/fe78a78911e2df9cdb488ec57b0e0a34bb56e18b57303d895dc8013b64a4afc3.png)\n\nApproximate the rate at which the temperature of the engine increases when $t = 3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nT'(t) \\approx \\dfrac{T(t+h) - T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{T(3+1)-T(3-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(4)-T(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{60-30}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of temperature increase is approximately $15^{\\circ}$ per minute."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3036234-bc7e-5e96-b02a-80edd92bdbbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337107} {:answer/id #uuid "04718383-ec61-5d5c-94de-6f03f0603706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337108} {:answer/id #uuid "991d0afd-0a94-5e0b-b85b-032097321c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337109} {:answer/id #uuid "447d8afa-f807-5765-9483-91b1e0741157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337110} {:answer/id #uuid "ad7066b9-1fb6-5c8c-9847-d350fa37fff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "991d0afd-0a94-5e0b-b85b-032097321c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337109} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fedd74f-c0bc-5a0a-acdd-b35d09ec210a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "719885bd-89ec-5a69-9a1b-0bb3396c2432" :question/math-academy-id "q-170649" :question/problem "Given that $f(2.9)=5.91$ and $f(3.1)=7.11,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(3).$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=3$ with the step size $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+0.1)-f(3-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3.1)-f(2.9)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7.11-5.91}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.2}{0.2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cbdf0a5-0c2c-5828-96b8-bae9b6e8b810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337114} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7543b7-4381-5d08-852c-6e301f6c3ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337115} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2374a3-1e7e-527a-892c-cbadd3e4456f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337116} {:answer/id #uuid "3bcab95d-d87b-5553-b53c-80f8fd95a303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337117} {:answer/id #uuid "92fb79b0-96e1-5306-b182-d1540785e12a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bcab95d-d87b-5553-b53c-80f8fd95a303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337117} :answer-field/id #uuid "eaea3169-febe-5711-b2ea-77433ce54a4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "610eb926-0dd8-506c-b3e0-57258913337a" :question/math-academy-id "q-170650" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/85aff149fcbad4437f64f7d6eab96a42a287417c6c8f5483a03bf6fc2f22b930.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+1)-g(4-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(5)-g(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73db0455-d7f7-5108-b2f1-cbfff41b387a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337121} {:answer/id #uuid "6bc6589b-018f-5f42-8f41-4a39d5454404" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337122} {:answer/id #uuid "9d5e0e09-d4b9-532a-a1d5-83e0baf68c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337123} {:answer/id #uuid "675c493c-c47b-574d-b67f-2160d79a51ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337124} {:answer/id #uuid "84aa0392-1a3e-5c3e-b5b8-8047aeeb6353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bc6589b-018f-5f42-8f41-4a39d5454404" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337122} :answer-field/id #uuid "19d61f57-8395-5793-bdbc-a86a924d2890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7eb6c7c-5b6e-50a1-b81c-4f076d395815" :question/math-academy-id "q-170651" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/7f36258f966a7af5ae9f35c4e3214bb8c2c7d0ae66039256b2484df5b34d83fb.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=3$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{g(3+1)-g(3-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(4)-g(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-4}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c788e050-6d29-52f3-ae00-ac57242deb8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c788e050-6d29-52f3-ae00-ac57242deb8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337128} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cbd34dd-c80f-5b10-bdca-f6db24f6ad5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07578661-317b-5244-989a-6d1ed375019c" :question/math-academy-id "q-315235" :question/problem "In a lab experiment, the temperature of a chemical reactor (in ${}^{∘}C$) after $t$ minutes is given by the function $T(t).$ The values of $T(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1.2$ | $1.6$ | $2.0$ | $2.4$ | $2.8$ | $3.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$T(t)$** | $28$ | $30$ | $32$ | $34$ | $35$ | $36$ |\n\nApproximate the reactor’s temperature instantaneous rate of change at $t=2.0$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.4.$\n\nThe reactor’s temperature at $t=2.0$ is changing at approximately \n{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}C$ per minute." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{T}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{T(t+h)-T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat time $t=2.0$ with step size $h=0.4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(2.0) & ≈\\frac{T(2.0+0.4)-T(2.0-0.4)}{2(0.4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(2.4)-T(1.6)}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{34-30}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{0.8} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the reactor’s temperature at $t=2.0$ is changing at approximately $5\\,{}^{∘}C$ per minute."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7b839a2-a641-5253-802a-0d8e3959e566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075915} {:answer/id #uuid "c483963e-57f9-5d4e-9222-ae0776f9ac4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075916} {:answer/id #uuid "1147e451-0584-572f-ad2b-ced4053053f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075917} {:answer/id #uuid "7a9de122-54df-5942-ad79-cbc266f5a635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075918} {:answer/id #uuid "7fef81f0-ea59-50f8-a66b-0437137410e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c483963e-57f9-5d4e-9222-ae0776f9ac4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075916} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3519576-a94b-5410-8340-1c167b379854" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db9edec3-4494-5ddd-9ed4-509fa1e568a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32535" :question/problem "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-1.05$ | $-1$ | $-0.95$ | $-0.9$ | $-0.85$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $3.4$ | $2.5$ | $1.6$ | $2.1$ | $2.7$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a central difference approximation." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.05.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{g(-1+0.05)-g(-1-0.05)}{2(0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(-0.95)-g(-1.05)}{2(0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.6-3.4}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.8}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18}{1} \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337129 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245651ef-31a2-5d02-bed3-6e53beb42f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337131} {:answer/id #uuid "3de6bdfa-fcb7-5e86-997e-3a7b91fa3214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3de6bdfa-fcb7-5e86-997e-3a7b91fa3214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337132} :answer-field/id #uuid "677f6bb2-95eb-531a-8c84-05368de32aa6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c795a3d5-0d99-504a-8cda-52da7f8df108" :question/math-academy-id "q-343970" :question/problem "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-5.0$ | $-4.0$ | $-2.7$ | $-1.0$ | $0.5$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a central difference approximation.\n\n${g}^{′}(-1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{g(-1+1)-g(-1-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(0)-g(-2)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.0-(-4.0)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ce26b7b-187c-5177-8b27-c3b41c237ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ce26b7b-187c-5177-8b27-c3b41c237ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337135} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cef763f-0b61-5770-8850-1c31be8e3ae4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "389ac68b-8463-52b0-bca0-00a5d659e825" :question/math-academy-id "q-343977" :question/problem "Given that $f(4.9)=3.12$ and $f(5.1)=2.36,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(5).$\n\n${f}^{′}(5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=5$ with the step size $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(5) & ≈\\frac{f(5+0.1)-f(5-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5.1)-f(4.9)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.36-3.12}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-0.76)}{0.2} \\\\  & =-3.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ad4d043-9f3a-5974-aaa6-a1af4a88dcb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ad4d043-9f3a-5974-aaa6-a1af4a88dcb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337138} :answer-field/id #uuid "c32dfa01-e8fe-55e5-9a1b-5271fb01221e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82c6adbb-7838-58fa-83a8-51e77b737ad5" :question/math-academy-id "q-344006" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/ab10c9d133e6a383439b0a8b89643564f5f438d061dba647288927102e870a1b.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=2.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=-3$ and $x=1.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(-1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{f(-1+2)-f(-1-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1)-f(-3)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)}{4} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45ab7e65-158e-506a-a9a2-64b23cb4f398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337141} {:answer/id #uuid "d2baed68-acb8-5c5c-887c-b940e5917530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2baed68-acb8-5c5c-887c-b940e5917530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337142} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4302dfb-d89c-5607-83af-9652adee36d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e7dcee7-67dd-5981-a383-761fa930ef45" :question/math-academy-id "q-344027" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/e4097b002333ba5b874632c61ecbb2b212235a1cc74912b2f74bcb5740e86e02.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=3$ and $x=5.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(4)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{f(4+1)-f(4-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5)-f(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-(-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "020b1e4f-a89f-53df-9e88-bfe48d9f3ead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337145} {:answer/id #uuid "228e7a40-7e1b-51f7-94c0-b7675831c2dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "228e7a40-7e1b-51f7-94c0-b7675831c2dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337146} :answer-field/id #uuid "104e562a-0667-5817-bbbc-d61083f8cd21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44c56c27-a6d5-502c-baaf-243795a3dee4" :question/math-academy-id "q-344341" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/28cef739fd66e414894e830a02582f979dfdf285b3208cff5bba42b68537eefa.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=8$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=2.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=6$ and $x=10.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(8)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=8$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(8) & ≈\\frac{f(8+2)-f(8-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(10)-f(6)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)}{4} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a72a384-ce71-59f7-9ab5-fbf72444ccda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337149} {:answer/id #uuid "7f986d2b-3fe3-508a-a119-3e16d283640e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a72a384-ce71-59f7-9ab5-fbf72444ccda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337149} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf61ad9f-a811-5fed-a894-e836b265d4d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec64348f-7276-56b9-abdf-72ec76221afc" :question/math-academy-id "q-344357" :question/problem "In an environmental study, the water level in a reservoir (in $m$) after $t$ hours is given by the function $W(t).$ The values of $W(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $0.8$ | $1.0$ | $1.2$ | $1.4$ | $1.6$ | $1.8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$W(t)$** | $5.6$ | $5.3$ | $5.0$ | $4.7$ | $4.2$ | $3.9$ |\n\nApproximate the reservoir’s water level's instantaneous rate of change at $t=1.4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.2.$\n\nThe reservoir’s water level at $t=1.4$ is decreasing at approximately \n{{field-1}} $m$ per hour." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{W(t+h)-W(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat time $t=1.4$ with step size $h=0.2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(1.4) & ≈\\frac{W(1.4+0.2)-W(1.4-0.2)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{W(1.6)-W(1.2)}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4.2-5.0}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-0.8}{0.4} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the reservoir’s water level at $t=1.4$ is decreasing at approximately $2\\,m$ per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae0f0af5-cae8-5a86-9695-b7dec452c6b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae0f0af5-cae8-5a86-9695-b7dec452c6b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337153} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a5b923-b80c-5608-8937-70eaf91cee7b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b099ac7-cdc4-5055-bbc0-2c4b0aca6b20" :question/math-academy-id "q-344361" :question/problem "In a medical study, the concentration of a drug in a patient’s bloodstream (in $mg/L$) after $t$ hours is given by the function $C(t).$ The values of $C(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $2.0$ | $2.4$ | $2.8$ | $3.2$ | $3.6$ | $4.0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$C(t)$** | $12.4$ | $11.8$ | $11.0$ | $10.4$ | $9.8$ | $9.2$ |\n\nApproximate the drug’s concentration instantaneous rate of change at $t=3.2$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.4.$\n\nThe drug’s concentration at $t=3.2$ is decreasing at approximately \n{{field-1}} $mg/L$ per hour." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{C}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{C(t+h)-C(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat time $t=3.2$ with step size $h=0.4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{′}(3.2) & ≈\\frac{C(3.2+0.4)-C(3.2-0.4)}{2(0.4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{C(3.6)-C(2.8)}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9.8-11.0}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1.2)}{0.8} \\\\  & =-1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the drug’s concentration at $t=3.2$ is decreasing at approximately $1.5\\,mg/L$ per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34deacc7-fe6a-5f63-a8e8-59dbeb887e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${16}^{∘}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337156} {:answer/id #uuid "a38ac727-e311-5a4b-8f43-23be410497b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${20}^{∘}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337157} {:answer/id #uuid "f30f5f9b-7bf9-5e08-ac1a-5408bcf5ee29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${8}^{∘}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337158} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a7bf0c-5cc5-5c7e-b6ac-2fe1efd7c9b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${4}^{∘}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337159} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8abf06-ed31-5b01-8473-5132f2cf283e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${40}^{∘}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a8abf06-ed31-5b01-8473-5132f2cf283e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${40}^{∘}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337160} :answer-field/id #uuid "c23268cd-5b30-571a-896a-a5cef4c880c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a5f3525-781f-598d-b562-9b3d6c7b6d32" :question/math-academy-id "q-47504" :question/problem "The temperature of a certain liquid under heating is given by the function $T(t),$ where $t$ is the time in hours. The values of $T(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1.2$ | $1.4$ | $1.6$ | $1.8$ | $2.0$ | $2.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T(t)$ | $-12$ | $-10$ | $-4$ | $6$ | $10$ | $13$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nDetermine the instantaneous temperature rate at the instant of time $t=1.6$ using a central difference approximation with the step size $h=0.2.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{T}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{T(t+h)-T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=1.6$ with step size $h=0.2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(1.6) & ≈\\frac{T(1.6+0.2)-T(1.6-0.2)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(1.8)-T(1.4)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-(-10)}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{0.4} \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous temperature rate at the instant of time $t=1.6$ is ${40}^{∘}$ per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "950be1fa-d2e6-5869-8fe4-496f9574b9cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337163} {:answer/id #uuid "028aee04-da3e-5a1c-89db-1aea3bf20029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.05\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337164} {:answer/id #uuid "92bc3d62-fa48-59ab-ae6a-a9ed02d7e52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337165} {:answer/id #uuid "da37e92f-5ca9-5f40-a7fa-8de6ce148be5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337166} {:answer/id #uuid "16f4c2f8-6949-5123-a838-977f4b1f2fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "950be1fa-d2e6-5869-8fe4-496f9574b9cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337163} :answer-field/id #uuid "63273c97-8f73-5984-8f3b-a68ff7a99ae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbfaa746-7592-59a4-b95e-aa048f2cedc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-51402" :question/problem "Sam wanted to estimate the rate of weight growth of his new puppy. He took note of its weight every week, for $7$ weeks. The results are shown in the table below, where $W(t)$ is the puppy's weight (measured in pounds) after $t$ weeks from birth.\n\n| **$t$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ | $14$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $W(t)$ | $9$ | $10.1$ | $11.3$ | $12.4$ | $13.5$ | $14.6$ | $15.8$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the puppy's rate of weight growth $12$ weeks after birth using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{W(t+h)-W(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=12$ and step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(0.2) & ≈\\frac{W(12+1)-W(12-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{W(13)-W(11)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14.6-12.4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.2}{2} \\\\  & =1.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the rate of weight growth at the instant of time $t=12$ is $1.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c54c5bd5-dd2c-587d-ad5a-b7f3b81a0873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337170} {:answer/id #uuid "7a528b19-6e26-5c94-b2dc-50692a554918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337171} {:answer/id #uuid "87ca8e76-54ee-5b96-bfa2-95a7af044cd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337172} {:answer/id #uuid "00ea89c8-2434-56da-8ed3-b6cfb5ad1d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337173} {:answer/id #uuid "8e74c3d8-349a-5cec-aca4-50b2539aea82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87ca8e76-54ee-5b96-bfa2-95a7af044cd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337172} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c021e07-db25-5c67-af01-a11ba734fb5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d330499c-93fb-5c00-84c7-735023ffba22" :question/math-academy-id "q-75121" :question/problem "Given that $f(9.6)=3$ and $f(10.4)=11,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(10).$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=10$ with the step size $h=0.4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(10) & ≈\\frac{f(10+0.4)-f(10-0.4)}{2(0.4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(10.4)-f(9.6)}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{11-3}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{0.8} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
